
## Setting no proxy

{{ provisioner_name }} runs its own internal proxy for services which may not
interact well if you run another httpd server. Here we set the no proxy variable
to prevent lookups. The list contains the service names as well as the head
node's own name and address, so that requests to local services never go
through a site proxy. The setting goes in a profile script, so every new login
shell on the head node has it too.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment OpenCHAMI no proxy settings -->
```bash
cat > /etc/profile.d/ohpc-openchami-noproxy.sh <<EOF
openchami_hosts="${sms_name},${sms_ip},localhost,127.0.0.1,smd,smd-init,\
boot-service,metadata-service,tokensmith,acme-deploy,acme-register,haproxy,\
postgres,step-ca,coresmd-coredhcp,coresmd-coredns"
EOF
cat >> /etc/profile.d/ohpc-openchami-noproxy.sh <<'EOF'
export no_proxy="${no_proxy:+${no_proxy},}${openchami_hosts}"
export NO_PROXY="${NO_PROXY:+${NO_PROXY},}${openchami_hosts}"
EOF
. /etc/profile.d/ohpc-openchami-noproxy.sh
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
